{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/689474-paranoia-of-typical-vascu-and-the-fbi","id":689474,"title":"Paranoia of typical VASCU (and the FBI)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-05T01:57:22-07:00","id":689474,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Paranoia of typical VASCU (and the FBI)","content":"At the moment I am running a Changeling campaign, and one of the fetches went over the deep end, fitting the slasher mold quit well. The fetch has drawn the attention of the VASCU and obviously the PCs run across the agents while doing their own investigation. I am a bit curious how paranoid the VASCU agents are and how easily they use their benedictions even when doing a quick id check. Obviously, I could simply pick what is best for the story, but I want to know how other storytellers feel about it.<br /> <br /> The agents accidentally met the PCs while the characters were acting somewhat odd at a semi-private parking spot which was the latest body dump site. The dump site had been cleaned out by CSI, but the characters were checking for 'magical' influences such as portal into the Hedge. Instead of the expected excuse of being lost tourists or something equally mundane, they began to sprout something about being bloggers and about the whole murder being a conspiracy of aliens and the government. The idea of the players was of course, to look like irritating harmless fools, but how harmless are those conspiracy theorists in a world were some of them are definitely true or that the PCs accidentally started behaving as another hunting organization? Obviously this lead to a quick id check. The IDs were at a first glance fine and the agents walked away rather irritated, but unwilling to cause a scene. The agents do have access to security camera footage though and as such combined with the names could do a rather intensive background check. Such a check would trigger alarm bells, since one of them used a shabby fake id, is suspected in a cold case and actually knew the victim. The other character is connected with the Italian mob, was recently accused of kidnapping (a misunderstand solved by an excellent lawyer) and the victim is Russian mob. But would under these circumstances the agents spend their precious resources on what at first glance appear to be a bunch of weird harmless people?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","user":"Madfox11","date":". 10-05-2015, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:17:15-07:00","id":689502,"title":"","content":"I think it's reasonable to go either way depending on exactly how convincing your players were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:31:10-07:00","id":689797,"title":"","content":"A big factor is just how suspicious your people were being. VASCU primarily goes after serial killers and slashers, but I can see them being seconded for mundane investigation as well. So the question becomes, as Michael said, how convincing your players were, and how much time and effort the agents are willing to invest in looking into these conspiracy theorists. If they mentioned anything about the government and psychics though, that's when VASCU will take a very concentrated interest to look into how, exactly, these people know about such things. If the VASCU agents are what you could call good cops they'll definitely run the names and IDs again through a few databases (and take a day or two at least) to turn up something. If they're harried and pressed for time they're leave it to someone else (taking at best a week) to run the information for them, but which time I'm gonna presume your changelings are gonna already be solving their problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:47:58-07:00","id":689905,"title":"","content":"VASCU running after fae? Answer is obvious...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.ablogforbetterbusiness.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/dirty-truth-about-network-marketing.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/